# SCOPED TO PINNED FIXTURES ONLY. This sets NO repository-wide line-ending policy.
#
# WHY IT EXISTS. `core.autocrlf` is true in this clone, so git strips CRs on commit. On
# 2026-09-04 that silently altered the two files whose entire purpose is byte-exactness:
#
#     gates/GATE16_C1_PINNED.html   disk 1,344,077 B -> blob 1,342,601 B   (-1,476)
#     removed/_new_SGLT2.html       disk 3,460,804 B -> blob 3,457,916 B   (-2,888)
#
#     A HASH RECORDED AGAINST A WORKING-TREE FILE IS NOT A HASH OF WHAT WAS COMMITTED
#     WHEN core.autocrlf IS ON. THE ACT OF PRESERVING THE BYTES CHANGED THEM.
#
# Both artefacts are identified BY THEIR HASH and nothing else -- one is a gate's pinned
# control, the other has unestablished authorship where the hash is its only identity --
# so a recorded hash a fresh clone cannot reproduce is a provenance failure even though
# neither gate's verdict changed (gate16 still PASSed, and its rot-guard would have caught
# a functional break).
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for these paths: the blob is the bytes.
gates/GATE16_C1_PINNED.html          -text
gates/GATE16_C1_PINNED_STORE.json    -text
gates/GATE16_NEG_PINNED.html         -text
gates/GATE16_NEG_PINNED_STORE.json   -text
removed/_new_SGLT2.html              -text

# ARCHIVED WITHDRAWALS, added 2026-09-09 -- THE SAME DEFECT, A THIRD TIME.
# Withdrawing SGLT2_MACE_CVOT_REVIEW.html archived the served page and the commit
# normalised it: disk 1,742,860 B -> blob 1,741,954 B (-906, exactly its CRLF count).
# The archive of a withdrawal exists so a reader can confirm WHAT WAS SERVED; a blob a
# fresh clone cannot reproduce byte-for-byte defeats the only purpose it has. Same class
# as the two fixtures above: identified by its bytes and nothing else.
archive/*.html                       -text
